  "question": {
    "text": "Two capacitors, each having capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> are connected in series. The space between one of the capacitors is filled with dielectric material of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> such that the equivalence capacitance of the system became <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> will be :",
    "image": null
  },
